/**
 * @addtogroup Foundation_BuildGuide_Overview
 *
 * Foundation supports three main usage modes:
 *
 * @section FoundationBuildSourceMode Source Mode
 *
 * Source mode uses the repository directly.
 *
 * This is the default mode for:
 *
 * - Arduino,
 * - development,
 * - debugging,
 * - changing feature macros,
 * - modifying Foundation internals.
 *
 * In source mode, Foundation remains fully configurable through compile-time macros.
 *
 * @section FoundationBuildFullPrecompiledMode Full Precompiled Mode
 *
 * Full precompiled mode builds Foundation with all supported modules enabled.
 *
 * This mode is intended for:
 *
 * - quick integration,
 * - desktop experiments,
 * - users that want a ready-to-link library,
 * - generic full builds for known toolchains.
 *
 * A full build is larger, but easier to consume.
 *
 * @section FoundationBuildCustomPrecompiledMode Custom Precompiled Mode
 *
 * Custom precompiled mode builds Foundation for a specific target, toolchain,
 * architecture, ABI, and feature set.
 *
 * This mode is intended for:
 *
 * - embedded targets,
 * - memory-constrained systems,
 * - production builds,
 * - projects that only need a subset of Foundation.
 *
 * @section FoundationBuildRule General Rule
 *
 * If macros change the compiled implementation, build a custom library.
 * If the project needs maximum flexibility, use source mode.
 * If the project needs fast integration, use a precompiled full build.
 */
